<[Leonard] NMORGENSTERN> He is setting up a bunch of Mac II's using Unix and 
Mac Forth.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Larry - what's going on in GA ?
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> RAIN and democrats
<[Gary] GARY-S> Send the rain - keep the poloticians
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> I get the HARRIS forth chip development system on Monday. 
I'm excited.
<[Leonard] NMORGENSTERN> Must'nt talk about politics, religion, or women.
<[Leonard] NMORGENSTERN> Therefore I have nothing to say.
<D.RUFFER> is here.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Why are you getting the set ?
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> no one home :-(
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> My company is HARRIS's second customer for the chips.
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> We plan on build systems around the chip.
<[Gary] GARY-S> are you beta testing or rolling something REAL ?
<[Leonard] NMORGENSTERN> How do you mean second? In time, or volume?
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> Time, we only ordered about 7 chips.
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> This is not beta stuff. We (Gerogia Tech) will upgrade our 
novix designs.
<[Gary] GARY-S> That should squeeze down the size of your controllers quite a 
bit, Larry
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> Yep, now our!Nubus cards will fit in MAC II.
<[Gary] GARY-S> do you also Hypercard ?
<[Leonard] NMORGENSTERN> What is Nubus?
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> Only for documentation-- NUBUS is bus in MAC II.
<[Gary] GARY-S> like a VME bus, Len
<[Leonard] NMORGENSTERN> Thanks
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> NUBUS is a magnitude simpler than VME in hardware.
<[Gary] GARY-S> it was a RUFF comparison - but I figured he could relate quickly
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> I'll have more info on harris stuff next week.
<[Gary] GARY-S> You know what I think would be great ? keep a running log 
(non-proprietary) of the development
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> BTW, Dr. William Dress appears in Popular Science. He uses 
Forth&Novix.
<[Gary] GARY-S> A lot of systems people would profit from your experiance
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> Ok about LOG. We document the $#%^ out of our stuff.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Bill Dress is a verrrry interesting person, but he flat refuses 
to get on GEnie !
<[Leonard] NMORGENSTERN> I think what Gary means is to write a history...
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> I visted Him at Oakridge a few months ago.
<[Leonard] NMORGENSTERN> of the development at some future time.
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> I keep a development diary (required at work) that would 
suffice.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Did you get a demo of his RealOps while there ?
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> RealOps is Laird William's mostly. I saw him too but didn't 
obtain the stuff.
<[Gary] GARY-S> The development library would be interesting Larry - thanks
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> When I stop working 90+ hours, Ill download things.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Lazy - worthless...... :-)
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> I'm just not motivated I guess.
<[Larry] L.DANIEL1> Forth si so dull sometimes :)
<[Leonard] NMORGENSTERN> When you quit working so hard, you can start...
<[Leonard] NMORGENSTERN> thinking about motivation.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Yeah - and rain is an overated commodity
<[Gary] GARY-S> Leonard lapses into philosophy on occassion - he assumes we all 
